A race of small, misshapen, dwarf-like creatures that dwell in the 
earth. The name 'gnome' was given to them by the medieval scholar 
Paracelcus, in an attempt to describe the most important of the earth 
spirits. Gnomes live under the earth, where they guard treasures. 
According to Paracelcus, they move as easily through the earth as 
humans walk upon the ground. They cannot stand the light of the sun, 
for even one ray would turn them to stone. Some sources claim they 
spend the hours during daylight as a toad. They are in some way related 
to goblins and dwarfs.

"Gnome." Encyclopedia Mythica from Encyclopedia Mythica Online.
<http://www.pantheon.org/articles/g/gnome.html>
[Accessed October 21, 2005].

